msgstr "Semua nod perantara (bulatan) bertanggungjawab untuk pelbagai jenis manipulasi data.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Query the required inputs and expected outputs {#query-the-required-inputs-and-expected-outputs}"
msgstr "Menyoal input yang diperlukan dan output yang dijangkakan {#query-the-required-inputs-and-expected-outputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The easiest way to see the required inputs and expected outputs is to print the [`Samplex`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex\") object. Array items are formatted as `'{name}' <{type}[{shape}...]>`, and the required inputs precede the optional inputs.\n"
msgstr "Cara paling mudah untuk melihat input yang diperlukan dan output yang dijangkakan ialah dengan mencetak objek [`Samplex`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex\"). Item tatasusunan diformatkan sebagai `'{name}' <{type}[{shape}...]>`, dan input yang diperlukan mendahului input pilihan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`inputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs\") and [`outputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs\") of the samplex, as well as more detailed information like their names, shapes, types, and descriptions, can also be queried programatically. The return type of both of these methods is a [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\"). For example, the following code lists all specifications of the input interface:\n"
msgstr "[`inputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs\") dan [`outputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs\") samplex, serta maklumat yang lebih terperinci seperti nama, bentuk, jenis dan perihalannya, juga boleh disoal secara programatik. Jenis pulangan kedua-dua kaedah ini ialah [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\"). Contohnya, kod berikut menyenaraikan semua spesifikasi antara muka input:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The next example prints some information about those output specifiers whose names contain the string `\"flips\"`.\n"
msgstr "Contoh seterusnya mencetak sedikit maklumat tentang spesifikasi output yang namanya mengandungi rentetan `\"flips\"`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bind input values and sample {#bind-input-values-and-sample}"
msgstr "Ikat nilai input dan sampel {#bind-input-values-and-sample}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\"), the samplex needs values for at least those [`inputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs\") that are marked as required. These values are first bound to an input interface so that it can perform all necessary type checking (or type coercion in some cases) and shape analysis. If anything is wrong with the types or shapes, or if a required value is missing, a verbose error is raised.\n"
msgstr "Untuk [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\"), samplex memerlukan nilai bagi sekurang-kurangnya [`inputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.inputs\") yang ditandakan sebagai diperlukan. Nilai ini mula-mula diikat kepada antara muka input supaya ia dapat melakukan semua semakan jenis yang diperlukan (atau paksaan jenis dalam sesetengah kes) dan analisis bentuk. Jika terdapat sesuatu yang salah pada jenis atau bentuk, atau jika nilai yang diperlukan tiada, ralat yang terperinci akan dibangkitkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bind input {#bind-input}"
msgstr "Ikat input {#bind-input}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the following example, the [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") method is passed the required input values. It is then used to draw three randomizations from the samplex. The required bindings from the dressings are the Pauli Lindblad maps for noise injection and the basis change array. Additionally, values for the four parameters in the original boxed circuit are required, which in this case is set to `np.linspace(0, 1, 4)`. The samplex composes these parameters into the dressings, so they effectively become modifications to the samplex’s output parameter values.\n"
msgstr "Dalam contoh berikut, kaedah [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") diberikan nilai input yang diperlukan. Ia kemudian digunakan untuk mengambil tiga perawakan daripada samplex. Pengikatan yang diperlukan daripada dressing ialah peta Pauli Lindblad untuk suntikan hingar dan tatasusunan pengubahan basis. Selain itu, nilai bagi empat parameter dalam litar ber-box asal diperlukan, yang dalam kes ini ditetapkan kepada `np.linspace(0, 1, 4)`. Samplex menggubah parameter ini ke dalam dressing, jadi ia secara berkesan menjadi pengubahsuaian kepada nilai parameter output samplex.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inputs can be bound to the interface through multiple calls to [`bind()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind\") or by direct item assignment. Despite the nested dictionary format that [`bind()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind\") allows for convenience, it is a flat mapping object, and supports all of the usual mapping syntax. Once all required inputs have been found, [`fully_bound`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.fully_bound \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.fully_bound\") becomes true.\n"
msgstr "Input boleh diikat kepada antara muka melalui beberapa panggilan [`bind()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind\") atau melalui penugasan item secara langsung. Walaupun format kamus bersarang yang dibenarkan oleh [`bind()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.bind\") demi kemudahan, ia ialah objek pemetaan rata, dan menyokong semua sintaks pemetaan biasa. Sebaik sahaja semua input yang diperlukan ditemui, [`fully_bound`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.fully_bound \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface.fully_bound\") menjadi benar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\") objects, including the [`SamplexOutput`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex-output#samplomatic.samplex.SamplexOutput \"samplomatic.samplex.SamplexOutput\") subclass, map objects against data that has been bound to them. This means that you can get, for example, the template parameter values as follows. In this case, it has shape `(3, 48)` since three randomizations were requested and the template circuit has 48 parameters.\n"
msgstr "Semua objek [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\"), termasuk subkelas [`SamplexOutput`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex-output#samplomatic.samplex.SamplexOutput \"samplomatic.samplex.SamplexOutput\"), memetakan objek kepada data yang telah diikat kepadanya. Ini bermakna anda boleh mendapatkan, sebagai contoh, nilai parameter templat seperti berikut. Dalam kes ini, ia mempunyai bentuk `(3, 48)` kerana tiga perawakan diminta dan litar templat mempunyai 48 parameter.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Specify input as a dictionary {#specify-input-as-a-dictionary}"
msgstr "Menentukan input sebagai kamus {#specify-input-as-a-dictionary}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instead of providing a fully-bound [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\"), you can specify the inputs as a standard dictionary, as is shown in the cell below. In this case, the [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") method internally binds the dictionary items to the samplex’s input interface to validate that all required inputs are present and compatible.\n"
msgstr "Sebagai ganti menyediakan [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\") yang terikat sepenuhnya, anda boleh menentukan input sebagai kamus piawai, seperti yang ditunjukkan dalam sel di bawah. Dalam kes ini, kaedah [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\") secara dalaman mengikat item kamus kepada antara muka input samplex untuk mengesahkan bahawa semua input yang diperlukan hadir dan serasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Input types {#input-types}"
msgstr "Jenis input {#input-types}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Currently, there are two interface value types:\n"
msgstr "Pada masa ini, terdapat dua jenis nilai antara muka:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Array-valued: These have a shape and a data type. Bound values are coerced into the data type if possible. Any dimension can be a free dimension.\n"
msgstr "Bernilai tatasusunan: Ini mempunyai bentuk dan jenis data. Nilai terikat dipaksa kepada jenis data jika boleh. Mana-mana dimensi boleh menjadi dimensi bebas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli Lindblad maps: These must be of type [`qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap) and must act on the prescribed number of qubits. The number of terms in the map is a free dimension.\n"
msgstr "Peta Pauli Lindblad: Ini mestilah berjenis [`qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap) dan mesti bertindak pada bilangan qubit yang ditetapkan. Bilangan sebutan dalam peta ialah dimensi bebas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Free dimensions {#free-dimensions}"
msgstr "Dimensi bebas {#free-dimensions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\") class has a notion of *free dimensions*, which are named integer sizes whose values are undetermined until some data has been bound to the interface that constrains them. All free dimensions of the same name must resolve to a consistent size when binding data, or an error will be raised. For example, in the [`outputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs\") of any samplex, the array axis corresponding to randomizations is a free parameter that has the name `\"num_randomizations\"` by convention. When `sample()` is called, it binds values to the outputs\n"
msgstr "Kelas [`TensorInterface`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/tensor-interface-tensor-interface#samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface \"samplomatic.tensor_interface.TensorInterface\") mempunyai konsep *dimensi bebas*, iaitu saiz integer bernama yang nilainya tidak ditentukan sehingga sesetengah data diikat kepada antara muka yang mengekangnya. Semua dimensi bebas yang bernama sama mesti diselesaikan kepada saiz yang konsisten apabila mengikat data, jika tidak ralat akan dibangkitkan. Contohnya, dalam [`outputs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.outputs\") mana-mana samplex, paksi tatasusunan yang sepadan dengan perawakan ialah parameter bebas yang bernama `\"num_randomizations\"` mengikut konvensyen. Apabila `sample()` dipanggil, ia mengikat nilai kepada output\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Another common free-dimension scenario is sharing term constraints between Pauli lindblad map specifications and their modifiers. A [`qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap) is an ordered sequence of terms, where each term contains a floating point rate and a sparse Pauli representation. The [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") function adds a specifier `\"pauli_lindblad_maps.<ref>\"` for this type for each [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\") annotation, and if it contains a `modifier_ref`, a `\"local_scales.<modifier_ref>\"` specifier is also added. Both of these share the free dimension `\"num_terms_<ref>\"` that specifies how many Pauli Lindblad terms are present in the noise model because the latter needs to zip against the rates of the former to scale them.\n"
msgstr "Satu lagi senario dimensi bebas yang lazim ialah perkongsian kekangan sebutan antara spesifikasi peta Pauli lindblad dan pengubahsuainya. [`qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap) ialah jujukan tertib sebutan, di mana setiap sebutan mengandungi kadar titik terapung dan perwakilan Pauli jarang. Fungsi [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") menambah penentu `\"pauli_lindblad_maps.<ref>\"` untuk jenis ini bagi setiap anotasi [`InjectNoise`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/inject-noise#samplomatic.InjectNoise \"samplomatic.InjectNoise\"), dan jika ia mengandungi `modifier_ref`, penentu `\"local_scales.<modifier_ref>\"` turut ditambah. Kedua-duanya berkongsi dimensi bebas `\"num_terms_<ref>\"` yang menentukan berapa banyak sebutan Pauli Lindblad yang terdapat dalam model hingar kerana yang kedua perlu dizip dengan kadar yang pertama untuk menskalakannya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qubit-ordering-convention\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qubit ordering convention {#qubit-ordering-convention}"
msgstr "Konvensyen susunan qubit {#qubit-ordering-convention}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Samplexes constructed from boxed circuits by the [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") function can require array-valued inputs to [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\"), where one index corresponds to qubits in a circuit’s box. This section explains the ordering convention that should be used for such axes. In summary: use the qubit order of the boxed circuit, restricted to the box’s qubits.\n"
msgstr "Samplex yang dibina daripada litar ber-box oleh fungsi [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") boleh memerlukan input bernilai tatasusunan kepada [`sample()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex.sample\"), di mana satu indeks sepadan dengan qubit dalam box litar. Bahagian ini menerangkan konvensyen susunan yang harus digunakan untuk paksi sedemikian. Ringkasnya: gunakan susunan qubit litar ber-box, terhad kepada qubit milik box.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, suppose you want to figure out how to specify a Pauli Lindblad map for `\"noise1\"`. Then the order of qubits in the noise map is with respect to these qubits:\n"
msgstr "Contohnya, andaikan anda ingin mengetahui cara menentukan peta Pauli Lindblad untuk `\"noise1\"`. Maka susunan qubit dalam peta hingar adalah berkenaan dengan qubit berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is, if you want `<Qubit register=(4, \"q0\"), index=2>` to be noisy with `X` noise, then you should define a Pauli Lindblad map like this one because it is at index `1` of `qubit_ordering_convention`.\n"
msgstr "Maksudnya, jika anda mahu `<Qubit register=(4, \"q0\"), index=2>` berhingar dengan hingar `X`, maka anda harus mentakrifkan peta Pauli Lindblad seperti ini kerana ia berada pada indeks `1` bagi `qubit_ordering_convention`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The same holds true for basis changes. If you want to rotate into the +1 eigenstates of the operators X, Y, and Z for qubits 0, 1, and 2 of `circuit`, respectively, then you should use the following array, recalling that the convention $I=0$, $Z=1$, $X=2$, and $Y=3$ is used in this library (and Qiskit).\n"
msgstr "Perkara yang sama berlaku untuk pengubahan basis. Jika anda mahu memutar ke dalam keadaan eigen +1 bagi pengendali X, Y dan Z untuk qubit 0, 1 dan 2 `circuit`, masing-masing, maka anda harus menggunakan tatasusunan berikut, sambil mengingati bahawa konvensyen $I=0$, $Z=1$, $X=2$, dan $Y=3$ digunakan dalam pustaka ini (dan Qiskit).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that the qubit ordering convention is *not* the order defined by either of the following:\n"
msgstr "Perhatikan bahawa konvensyen susunan qubit *bukan* susunan yang ditakrifkan oleh mana-mana daripada yang berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`box_instruction.qubits`, where `box_instruction` is a [`qiskit.circuit.CircuitInstruction`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.CircuitInstruction) whose operation is a [`qiskit.circuit.BoxOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.BoxOp), because the order of this list of qubits might depend on the order in which instructions were added to the box context, which would be a confusing convention. For example, `with box(): circuit.x([0, 1])` and `with box(): circuit.x([1, 0])` would result in different orderings.\n"
msgstr "`box_instruction.qubits`, di mana `box_instruction` ialah [`qiskit.circuit.CircuitInstruction`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.CircuitInstruction) yang operasinya ialah [`qiskit.circuit.BoxOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.BoxOp), kerana susunan senarai qubit ini mungkin bergantung pada susunan arahan ditambah ke dalam konteks box, yang akan menjadi konvensyen yang mmengelirukan. Contohnya, `with box(): circuit.x([0, 1])` dan `with box(): circuit.x([1, 0])` akan menghasilkan susunan yang berbeza.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`box_instruction.operation.body.qubits` because these qubits might not even appear in the outer circuit. Qubits inside the actual body of `BoxOp` instructions (or any other control flow operation like `IfElseOp`) are only promised to have a consisent meaning within that scope. This would be an ill-defined convention, and hard to use in general.\n"
msgstr "`box_instruction.operation.body.qubits` kerana qubit ini mungkin tidak muncul pun dalam litar luar. Qubit di dalam badan sebenar arahan `BoxOp` (atau operasi aliran kawalan lain seperti `IfElseOp`) hanya dijamin mempunyai makna yang konsisten dalam skop tersebut. Ini akan menjadi konvensyen yang tidak jelas takrifannya, dan sukar digunakan secara amnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Local testing with the template circuit {#local-testing-with-the-template-circuit}"
msgstr "Pengujian setempat dengan litar templat {#local-testing-with-the-template-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a [`Samplex`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex\") is constructed by using the [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\") function, the output parameter values should be directly compatible with the parameters of the associated template circuit. For example, you can bind values for one of the randomizations to the template for local inspection.\n"
msgstr "Jika [`Samplex`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/samplex-samplex#samplomatic.samplex.Samplex \"samplomatic.samplex.Samplex\") dibina dengan menggunakan fungsi [`build()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/samplomatic/auto/build#samplomatic.build \"samplomatic.build\"), nilai parameter output harus serasi secara langsung dengan parameter litar templat yang berkaitan. Contohnya, anda boleh mengikat nilai bagi salah satu perawakan kepada templat untuk pemeriksaan setempat.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/1d82c46209f8648a2df572cfef8ca256f47952566d34386761ab942aa6e50afd.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/1d82c46209f8648a2df572cfef8ca256f47952566d34386761ab942aa6e50afd.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/1d82c46209f8648a2df572cfef8ca256f47952566d34386761ab942aa6e50afd.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/1d82c46209f8648a2df572cfef8ca256f47952566d34386761ab942aa6e50afd.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This lets you verify that the samplex is outputing samples that are expected. For example, the following code casts the bound circuit to a [`qiskit.quantum_info.Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) object and composes with the bitflip Paulis to visually inspect that all three randomizations are logically equivalent to the base circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ini membolehkan anda mengesahkan bahawa samplex mengeluarkan sampel yang dijangkakan. Contohnya, kod berikut menukar litar terikat kepada objek [`qiskit.quantum_info.Operator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.Operator) dan menggubah dengan Pauli pembalikan bit untuk memeriksa secara visual bahawa ketiga-tiga perawakan setara secara logik dengan litar asas.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/af1aa74f8a0e8abed673d4cd43ff8b810c44297d2f3a42fcfb49ade811e51c58.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/af1aa74f8a0e8abed673d4cd43ff8b810c44297d2f3a42fcfb49ade811e51c58.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/af1aa74f8a0e8abed673d4cd43ff8b810c44297d2f3a42fcfb49ade811e51c58.png](/docs/images/addons/samplomatic/af1aa74f8a0e8abed673d4cd43ff8b810c44297d2f3a42fcfb49ade811e51c58.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Similarly, the following code passes output parameter values and the template to a sampler to simulate 10,000 shots of all randomizations, and compares the resulting expectation values (only of the alpha register) to the expectation values of a base circuit simulation.\n"
msgstr "Begitu juga, kod berikut menghantar nilai parameter output dan templat kepada sampler untuk mensimulasikan 10,000 shot bagi semua perawakan, dan membandingkan nilai jangkaan yang terhasil (hanya bagi register alpha) dengan nilai jangkaan simulasi litar asas.\n"
